From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NXForge layer <layer@nxforge.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:04:24 +0000
Subject: drs-headroom: Ocarina's dynamic resolution can keep part of the frame
 free

The level stub's climb compared each level's measured load with the game's
threshold (83, about 16.4 ms of 16.7), so on an M4 Pro it settled right at
the edge and a heavier moment held the frame step at 2 vsyncs. With
DM_DRS_HEADROOM=<percent> (0 to 30; the loader writes it as a float at
state +0x44) the stub lowers the threshold by that share:
ldr s2,[x16,#0x44]; fmsub s1,s1,s2,s1. 0 or unset keeps the game's. A
settings row (Resolution headroom: None, Some 5, More 10, Most 20) shows
under Dynamic resolution on builds with the DRS_HEADROOM capability.
