@@ -34,6 +34,10 @@ Ocarina of Time also offers **40 fps**, on the iPhone and the Mac. Each frame st
 
 Off, the default, keeps the 3D picture at full size. On lets the game lower its resolution when frames run heavy and raise it again when they fit, as on the Switch: steadier frame rate, at times a softer picture. Only games whose resolution control the app can hold offer it (NieR:Automata, Ocarina of Time).
 
+### Resolution headroom
+
+`DM_DRS_HEADROOM`, None by default, shown under Dynamic resolution while it is on, for games whose build has the stub (Ocarina of Time; NXForge). Some (5), More (10) and Most (20) lower the load the climb allows by that share of the frame, so it settles one or two levels lower and a heavier moment has GPU time to spare instead of dropping to 30 fps. On an M4 Pro, Ocarina at full load sat right at the game's threshold (about 16.4 ms of 16.7) with a hold at 2 vsyncs about every 17 seconds (2026-11-11).
+
 ### Render scale
 
 The size of the 3D picture, from 50 to 100 %. Below 100 % the size is fixed there and the game's own dynamic resolution is off; 100 % keeps the game's own. Lower can be lighter on the GPU but is blurrier; the HUD and text keep their sharpness. Only games the app can scale offer it.
